    "extracted_answer": "[1/2, '\\\\frac{1}{2}']",
    "gold_answer": "We have \\[1 = \\log(xy^{3}) = \\log x + 3\\log y \\quad\\text{and}\\quad 1 = \\log(x^{2}y) = 2\\log x + \\log y.\\]Solving yields $\\log x = \\frac{2}{5}$ and $\\log y = \\frac{1}{5}$. Thus \\[\\log(xy) = \\log x + \\log y = \\boxed{\\frac{3}{5}}.\\]",
